This conversation didn't start this year.

1550
01:20:52.128 --> 01:20:54.907
As a district, we've been talking about inequity for a long time.

1551
01:20:55.668 --> 01:20:59.408
And as was said in the Dyer listening session, sometimes it is more painful to

1552
01:20:59.428 --> 01:21:02.448
stretch change out over years than it is to move forward with intention.

1553
01:21:03.348 --> 01:21:06.508
I also want to acknowledge what I'm hearing from others, from families of students

1554
01:21:06.548 --> 01:21:10.428
with special needs who are worried about losing consistency, from educators who are

1555
01:21:10.448 --> 01:21:14.308
reeling from staffing cuts and uncertainty, and from families who are asking for

1556
01:21:14.348 --> 01:21:17.248
clarity about what this will mean for their children.

1557
01:21:17.288 --> 01:21:19.418
Those concerns are real, and they deserve to be heard.

1558
01:21:20.088 --> 01:21:23.108
At the same time, I think we have to be equally honest about something else.

1559
01:21:23.328 --> 01:21:25.968
The inequities between our schools are real.

1560
01:21:26.008 --> 01:21:29.958
When some classrooms have 13 students and others have over 20, that is not

1561
01:21:30.008 --> 01:21:33.818
equity. When access to programs and services varies widely between

1562
01:21:33.848 --> 01:21:37.328
schools, that's not equity. And when some students experience

1563
01:21:37.388 --> 01:21:41.018
stability and proximity while others face greater disruption, that's not

1564
01:21:41.068 --> 01:21:44.848
equity. And right now, the burden of this decision is not being

1565
01:21:44.868 --> 01:21:48.848
shared equitably. The Caylor community is being asked to carry the weight

1566
01:21:48.888 --> 01:21:52.837
of change largely on their own, losing their school, their community, and their

1567
01:21:52.928 --> 01:21:56.908
sense of stability while many other schools, including my own, appear at

1568
01:21:56.948 --> 01:21:59.548
this point to remain relatively unchanged.

1569
01:22:00.308 --> 01:22:03.988
As we delay reconfiguration, that imbalance only deepens.

1570
01:22:04.048 --> 01:22:07.208
The most meaningful way to support the Caylor community would have been to not

1571
01:22:07.228 --> 01:22:11.057
prolong uncertainty but to move forward together so that that change was shared and

1572
01:22:11.068 --> 01:22:13.668
so that all students could benefit from a more equitable system.

1573
01:22:14.528 --> 01:22:17.798
I say this with care because I'm part of a community that benefits from some of

1574
01:22:17.848 --> 01:22:20.648
these advantages. My children have thrived at Dyer.

1575
01:22:20.688 --> 01:22:23.688
We love our school, our teachers, and our neighborhood.

1576
01:22:23.708 --> 01:22:26.678
But loving the school and our neighborhood and committing to the well-being of our

1577
01:22:26.688 --> 01:22:28.828
entire district should not be in conflict.

1578
01:22:29.368 --> 01:22:31.188
If anything, it asks more of us.

1579
01:22:32.228 --> 01:22:35.398
It asks us to recognize that meaningful change is often uncomfortable-

1580
01:22:35.408 --> 01:22:35.948
30 seconds left

1581
01:22:36.248 --> 01:22:39.128
... and that that discomfort alone is not a reason to stop.

1582
01:22:39.868 --> 01:22:43.728
So if the board chooses to delay this decision, I urge you, do not let this become

1583
01:22:43.768 --> 01:22:47.748
